{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"tokens","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tokens"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A token is a named value your styles refer to. In Kirana it is an ordinary\nimported constant, so your editor shows the value, \"go to definition\" works, and\nnothing needs code generation."}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"import { defineTokens } from \"@kirana-style/core\"\n\nexport const space = defineTokens(\"space\", {\n  1: \"0.25rem\",\n  2: \"0.5rem\",\n  4: \"1rem\",\n})\n\ncss({ gap: space[2] })","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">import</span> { defineTokens } <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;@kirana-style/core&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> space = <span class=\"th-token th-function\">defineTokens</span>(<span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;space&quot;</span>, {\n  <span class=\"th-token th-number\">1</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;0.25rem&quot;</span>,\n  <span class=\"th-token th-number\">2</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;0.5rem&quot;</span>,\n  <span class=\"th-token th-number\">4</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;1rem&quot;</span>,\n})\n\n<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">gap</span>: space[<span class=\"th-token th-number\">2</span>] })"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first argument is the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"namespace"}]},{"type":"text","value":". It has to be unique in a package: two\ngroups claiming one namespace is an error ("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"token-namespace-collision","source":"token-namespace-collision"}},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A token's identity carries its package, so packages may each have a "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"theme","source":"theme"}},{"type":"text","value":" group\nand compile to different variables, which keeps libraries from overwriting each\nother's. Because they then read alike, the compiler points such a pair out with an\ninfo ("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"token-namespace-shared","source":"token-namespace-shared"}},{"type":"text","value":"), and "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span> <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">export</span>","source":"kirana-style export"}},{"type":"text","value":" names each token's\npackage."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"inlined-or-a-custom-property","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inlined or a custom property"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default a token is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"inlined"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"gap: space<span class=\"th-token th-string\">[2]</span>","source":"gap: space[2]"}},{"type":"text","value":" compiles to "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"gap: <span class=\"th-token th-number\">0.5</span>rem","source":"gap: 0.5rem"}},{"type":"text","value":". The\ntoken costs nothing, and unreferenced tokens emit nothing at all."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ask for a custom property when the value must be "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"overridable at runtime"}]},{"type":"text","value":", for a\ntheme, a mode, or a value a parent hands down:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"export const theme = defineTokens(\n  \"theme\",\n  { surface: \"white\", text: \"black\" },\n  { variable: true }\n)","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> theme = <span class=\"th-token th-function\">defineTokens</span>(\n  <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;theme&quot;</span>,\n  { <span class=\"th-token th-property\">surface</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;white&quot;</span>, <span class=\"th-token th-property\">text</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;black&quot;</span> },\n  { <span class=\"th-token th-property\">variable</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-literal\">true</span> }\n)"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Now "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"theme.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">surface</span>","source":"theme.surface"}},{"type":"text","value":" compiles to "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">var</span>(<span class=\"th-token th-variable\">--k</span>…)","source":"var(--k…)"}},{"type":"text","value":", the defaults are declared once in the\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"kirana.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">tokens</span>","source":"kirana.tokens"}},{"type":"text","value":" layer, and anything below can override them."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inlined"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"variable: true","source":"variable: true"}}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compiles to"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the literal value"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">var</span>(<span class=\"th-token th-variable\">--k</span>…)","source":"var(--k…)"}}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overridable at runtime"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"no"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cost"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"one declaration per token used"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use for"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"scales: spacing, radii, type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"themes, modes, values handed down"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"per-mode-values","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-mode values"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A token can carry a light and a dark value:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"export const theme = defineTokens(\n  \"theme\",\n  { surface: { light: \"white\", dark: \"oklch(0.21 0 0)\" } },\n  { variable: true }\n)","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> theme = <span class=\"th-token th-function\">defineTokens</span>(\n  <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;theme&quot;</span>,\n  { <span class=\"th-token th-property\">surface</span>: { <span class=\"th-token th-property\">light</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;white&quot;</span>, <span class=\"th-token th-property\">dark</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;oklch(0.21 0 0)&quot;</span> } },\n  { <span class=\"th-token th-property\">variable</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-literal\">true</span> }\n)"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Colours are usually better written as one "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">light-dark</span>()","source":"light-dark()"}},{"type":"text","value":" value, which needs no\nvariable at all and no mode plumbing. Use "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"{ light, dark }","source":"{ light, dark }"}},{"type":"text","value":" for values\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">light-dark</span>()","source":"light-dark()"}},{"type":"text","value":" cannot express, such as a shadow's opacity, a blend mode or an\nimage filter. "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tokens/themes-and-modes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Themes and modes"}]},{"type":"text","value":" covers the difference."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"registered-tokens","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Registered tokens"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Give a token a syntax and it becomes a real registered property, which means the\nbrowser can animate it:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"export const fade = defineTokens(\"fade\", {\n  stop: { value: \"0%\", syntax: \"<length-percentage>\", inherits: false },\n})","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> fade = <span class=\"th-token th-function\">defineTokens</span>(<span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;fade&quot;</span>, {\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">stop</span>: { <span class=\"th-token th-property\">value</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;0%&quot;</span>, <span class=\"th-token th-property\">syntax</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;&lt;length-percentage&gt;&quot;</span>, <span class=\"th-token th-property\">inherits</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-literal\">false</span> },\n})"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This emits "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"@property","source":"@property"}},{"type":"text","value":", and the token may then be used as a keyframe key."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With the universal syntax a token may have no value at all. It starts unset, and\nevery reference to it falls back to nothing ("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">var</span>(<span class=\"th-token th-variable\">--k</span>…,)","source":"var(--k…,)"}},{"type":"text","value":"), so a chain of such\ntokens lists only the parts an element sets. That is how Tailwind composes\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"filter","source":"filter"}},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"export const step = defineTokens(\"step\", {\n  blur: { syntax: \"*\", inherits: false },\n  grey: { syntax: \"*\", inherits: false },\n})\n\ncss({\n  [step.grey]: \"grayscale(100%)\",\n  filter: `${step.blur} ${step.grey}`, // grayscale(100%)\n})","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> step = <span class=\"th-token th-function\">defineTokens</span>(<span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;step&quot;</span>, {\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">blur</span>: { <span class=\"th-token th-property\">syntax</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;*&quot;</span>, <span class=\"th-token th-property\">inherits</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-literal\">false</span> },\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">grey</span>: { <span class=\"th-token th-property\">syntax</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;*&quot;</span>, <span class=\"th-token th-property\">inherits</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-literal\">false</span> },\n})\n\n<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({\n  [step.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">grey</span>]: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;grayscale(100%)&quot;</span>,\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">filter</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">`</span><span class=\"th-token th-operator\">${</span>step.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">blur</span><span class=\"th-token th-operator\">}</span><span class=\"th-token th-string\"> </span><span class=\"th-token th-operator\">${</span>step.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">grey</span><span class=\"th-token th-operator\">}</span><span class=\"th-token th-string\">`</span>, <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// grayscale(100%)</span>\n})"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tokens-nothing-uses","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tokens nothing uses"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A production build writes a variable token's declaration only when something uses\nit. That means a rule that reads it, or the finished JavaScript still naming it, as\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"el.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">style</span>.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">color</span> = theme.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">text</span>","source":"el.style.color = theme.text"}},{"type":"text","value":" does. A design system can define a hundred variable\ntokens, and a page that reads ten ships ten."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A token read by code the compiler never sees needs saying so. Examples: a plain\nscript, a server-only template, a third party. Declare it "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"runtime: true","source":"runtime: true"}},{"type":"text","value":", for one\ntoken or the whole group, and it is always written:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"export const brand = defineTokens(\n  \"brand\",\n  { accent: \"oklch(0.7 0.15 150)\" },\n  { runtime: true }\n)","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> brand = <span class=\"th-token th-function\">defineTokens</span>(\n  <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;brand&quot;</span>,\n  { <span class=\"th-token th-property\">accent</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;oklch(0.7 0.15 150)&quot;</span> },\n  { <span class=\"th-token th-property\">runtime</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-literal\">true</span> }\n)"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"runtime: true","source":"runtime: true"}},{"type":"text","value":" implies "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"variable: true","source":"variable: true"}},{"type":"text","value":". If code rendered after the stylesheet\nnames a token it left out, as a server-only component can, the build stops and\nnames the token, so a missing declaration never reaches a page."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The dev server, "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span> check","source":"kirana-style check"}},{"type":"text","value":" and bundlers other than Vite and Rolldown\nwrite every variable token, as before."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"a-token-as-a-style-key","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A token as a style key"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A variable token can be the "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"key"}]},{"type":"text","value":" of a declaration, which sets that custom\nproperty for the subtree:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"css({ [ctx.iconSize]: \"0.875rem\" })","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ [ctx.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">iconSize</span>]: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;0.875rem&quot;</span> })"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"That is how a control tells the icons inside it how big to be, without either side\nknowing the other's class names."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-the-compiler-checks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What the compiler checks"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A token that does not exist: "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"unknown-token","source":"unknown-token"}},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A token reference computed at runtime: "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"dynamic-token","source":"dynamic-token"}},{"type":"text","value":", since tokens are\nbuild-time values by design."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"defineTheme","source":"defineTheme"}},{"type":"text","value":" on a token that is not a custom property: "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"token-not-variable","source":"token-not-variable"}},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tokens/preset-scales","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using the scales preset"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Tailwind's vocabulary,\nready to import."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tokens/semantic-tokens","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Semantic tokens"}]},{"type":"text","value":": building your own layer on\ntop."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"tokens","text":"Tokens","level":1},{"id":"inlined-or-a-custom-property","text":"Inlined or a custom property","level":2},{"id":"per-mode-values","text":"Per-mode values","level":2},{"id":"registered-tokens","text":"Registered tokens","level":2},{"id":"tokens-nothing-uses","text":"Tokens nothing uses","level":2